# apocalypse-soak-start.vrs: apocalypse D30 (a run of hours), its start. The dev events.json holds apo-soak from
# fixtures/apo-soak.json: zombie-apocalypse with a Point goal 6 km off the map's east edge and marchSpeed 0.5, so no
# horde can reach it in 3 h and no player is needed for the hordes to march. Chaos starts it from his castle and leaves;
# the orchestrator closes the client, samples state.json's write time every 20 s, and after at least 3 h copies the
# logs, stops the event and reads them (renewal per living unit, rises on time, no [Error]/[Warning] of ours, caps).
console TPHome
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 ( timeout=40
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-soak
expect-log event apo-soak started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-soak hotspots: 3 \( timeout=10
expect-log apocalypse apo-soak roamers: \+[0-9]+ at hotspot 3 timeout=60
